@model Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html.IHtmlContent?
@*
    DfE Header (Rebrand): the GOV.UK Header component with the DfE logo in place of the
    GOV.UK logotype. See https://design.education.gov.uk/design-system/govuk-rebrand/dfe-header-rebrand

    This is hand-written GOV.UK Frontend header markup. The <govuk-header> tag helper always
    renders the GOV.UK logotype, and <govuk-generic-header> renders a black band, not the
    brand-colour band of the GOV.UK Header.

    The model is optional. It is the account navigation (the sign in or sign out links),
    which shows on the right of the band. A layout with no account links passes model="null".
    It must not leave the attribute out: a partial with no model attribute inherits the page's
    model, and that is never an IHtmlContent.

    The header renders a plain <div>. Each layout wraps this partial in <header role="banner">.
*@
<div class="govuk-header">
    <div class="govuk-header__container govuk-width-container app-header__container">
        <div class="govuk-header__logo">
            <a href="https://gov.uk/" class="govuk-header__homepage-link">
                <img src="~/images/department-for-education_white.png" alt="Department for Education" class="govuk-header__logotype">
            </a>
        </div>
        @Model
    </div>
</div>
